1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,950
If your boss said "use AI more"

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,950
and your body heard "don't mess this up" —

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,950
you're not slow.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,950
You're missing a map.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,950
Today: one idea, one skill, one action.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,950
Clarity on what AI may touch — and what stays human.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,575
Picture this.

8
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:48,200
In a Johannesburg office — or a school staffroom in Limpopo —

9
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:53,825
someone in leadership drops a line in the group chat:

10
00:00:53,875 --> 00:00:59,450
"Let's start using AI to work smarter.

11
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:05,075
"

12
00:01:05,125 --> 00:01:10,700
No policy.

13
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:16,325
No examples.

14
00:01:16,375 --> 00:01:21,950
No "never do this" list.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,575
Half the room freezes.

16
00:01:27,625 --> 00:01:33,200
Someone experiments wildly.

17
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:38,825
Someone pretends they already know.

18
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:44,450
I've watched excellent admins, teachers, supervisors, and analysts

19
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:50,075
get stuck between looking progressive and staying safe.

20
00:01:50,125 --> 00:01:55,700
Here's the truth:

21
00:01:55,750 --> 00:02:01,325
permission anxiety is not laziness.

22
00:02:01,375 --> 00:02:06,950
It's what happens when expectations arrive without boundaries.

23
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:14,009
The problem isn't AI at work.

24
00:02:14,059 --> 00:02:21,068
The problem is vague instruction without a use map.

25
00:02:21,118 --> 00:02:28,126
Ambiguity feels like danger —

26
00:02:28,176 --> 00:02:35,185
so people either avoid AI completely

27
00:02:35,235 --> 00:02:42,244
or use it in the riskiest places because those tasks feel urgent.

28
00:02:42,294 --> 00:02:49,303
So let's separate three lanes:

29
00:02:49,353 --> 00:02:56,362
One — Automate: repeatable formatting, sorting, first-pass

30
00:02:56,412 --> 00:03:03,421
cleanup where rules are clear.

31
00:03:03,471 --> 00:03:10,479
Two — Assist: drafts, summaries, outlines you will verify and own.

32
00:03:10,529 --> 00:03:17,538
Three — Avoid: passwords, confidential data, invented facts,

33
00:03:17,588 --> 00:03:24,597
final decisions, anything your role is accountable for without

34
00:03:24,647 --> 00:03:31,656
review.

35
00:03:31,706 --> 00:03:38,715
AI can speed preparation.

36
00:03:38,765 --> 00:03:45,774
AI cannot carry your accountability.

37
00:03:45,824 --> 00:03:52,832
Your judgment stays.

38
00:03:52,882 --> 00:03:59,891
That's not old-fashioned.

39
00:03:59,941 --> 00:04:06,950
That's professional.

40
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,167
Here's the skill.

41
00:04:12,217 --> 00:04:17,385
Framework name: THE WORK MAP

42
00:04:17,435 --> 00:04:22,602
Step 1 — Automate.

43
00:04:22,652 --> 00:04:27,820
List duties that are repetitive and low-risk:

44
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:33,037
rename files to a pattern, clean a table layout, turn bullet

45
00:04:33,087 --> 00:04:38,254
notes into a first agenda.

46
00:04:38,304 --> 00:04:43,472
If a mistake is easy to spot and easy to fix, it may belong here.

47
00:04:43,522 --> 00:04:48,689
Step 2 — Assist.

48
00:04:48,739 --> 00:04:53,907
List duties where AI can draft and you must decide:

49
00:04:53,957 --> 00:04:59,124
emails, report outlines, lesson activity ideas, meeting summaries.

50
00:04:59,174 --> 00:05:04,341
Rule: AI starts · you verify · you send.

51
00:05:04,391 --> 00:05:09,559
Step 3 — Avoid.

52
00:05:09,609 --> 00:05:14,776
List duties AI must not touch unsupervised:

53
00:05:14,826 --> 00:05:19,993
passwords, payroll details, medical or learner private data,

54
00:05:20,043 --> 00:05:25,211
legal commitments, performance judgments, anything you'd be

55
00:05:25,261 --> 00:05:30,428
ashamed to say "the tool made up.

56
00:05:30,478 --> 00:05:35,646
"

57
00:05:35,696 --> 00:05:40,863
Then pick one Assist duty and run it today —

58
00:05:40,913 --> 00:05:46,080
with a human check on facts before anyone else sees it.

59
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:51,298
That is the Work Map.

60
00:05:51,348 --> 00:05:56,515
Automate. Assist. Avoid.

61
00:05:56,565 --> 00:06:01,733
You stop guessing what's allowed —

62
00:06:01,783 --> 00:06:06,950
and you practise boss-safe clarity.

63
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:12,950
Quick psychology — not as a diagnosis, as a tool.

64
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:18,950
Ambiguity activates threat systems.

65
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:24,950
When rules are unclear, your brain overestimates punishment.

66
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:30,950
A written map shrinks the threat.

67
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,950
You replace "What if I get in trouble?

68
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:42,950
"

69
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:48,950
with "This duty is Assist — here's my check.

70
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:54,950
"

71
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:00,950
Ambiguity feels like danger.

72
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,950
Labels make action possible.

73
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:12,664
Your action today — under thirty minutes:

74
00:07:12,714 --> 00:07:18,379
1. Write eight duties you actually did this week.

75
00:07:18,429 --> 00:07:24,093
2. Label each Automate, Assist, or Avoid.

76
00:07:24,143 --> 00:07:29,807
3. Run one Assist task with AI — then verify names, numbers,

77
00:07:29,857 --> 00:07:35,521
and tone before you share.

78
00:07:35,571 --> 00:07:41,236
When you're done, you will not have a company policy.

79
00:07:41,286 --> 00:07:46,950
You will have a personal Work Map you can defend calmly.

80
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,950
If this helped, subscribe to FutureHer —

81
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,950
and take this week's challenge:

82
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:01,950
one Assist task a day, verified before send.

83
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:06,950
Join The Forward Collective if you want peers practising the same map.

84
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:15,950
Next time: prompting basics that still work in five years —

85
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:24,950
so your asks stop producing fluff.
